16:47:12.469 | A noxious, red-hued fog overwhelms the area with a thick, palpable vapour. Within the confines of this extraordinary shop, Vashnarian marble walls rise with an air of regal magnificence, the very essence of opulence etched into their every contour. A sumptuous rug in rich, dark red colours adorns the polished darkwood floor. A resplendent red and gold dragon is set into the walls in crushed rubies and molten gold, weaving sinuously around the four walls, like a guardian of the treasures within. Many flickering candles of varied sizes, set into sconces high above, cast a warm glow upon the space. The insignia of Mhaldor has been triumphantly imprinted upon the walls in gleaming gold, an emblem of authority intertwined with daemonic inscriptions that invoke an ancient language tied to the city's proud history. Alongside one wall, a formidable counter hewn from solid stone cradles a captivating array of rare goods. Unusual crystal and glass jars, refracting light into a kaleidoscope of colours, find their place upon its surface, promising treasures beyond the imagination. There are 5 Blackrock clerics here. A runic totem is planted solidly in the ground. A sigil in the shape of a small, rectangular monolith is on the ground. Lying flat on the ground is a key-shaped sigil. A daemonic hyena awaits in savage readiness, golden eyes burning with a cold, cunning malevolence amidst the steady exhalation of crimson fog from slavering jaws. An obsidian eye sigil is here. Its flat surface displaying countless runes, a mirror-like servitor hovers nearby. Exuding umbral menace, a phantom jaguar is crouched here. There are 2 hearts of a mortal, still dripping blood here. Commandant Saibel Aristata is here, hidden. Her features are obscured by a red wyvern mask. She wields Agith'maal's ire in her left hand and a sable shield webbed in silver damascene in her right.  You see a sign indicating there are WARES for sale here.
